# Gram-Schmidt Lesson & Visual Enhancements

This plan covers the creation of a high-fidelity Gram-Schmidt Orthogonalization lesson, leveraging the newly integrated `manim-web` engine. It also includes the necessary architectural improvements to support advanced vector operations like projections and subtractions.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Vector Animations**: The Gram-Schmidt process relies on visualizing projections. I will implement a new `project` animation in `ManimController` that draws a "projection line" (dashed) from the source vector to the target vector.
> **State Persistence**: The lesson will use incremental `add` and `animate` steps. If the user skips ahead, `resolveStateAtBeat` will ensure the final vectors are correctly placed.

## Proposed Changes

